  "instruction": "Rosalind Achterberg is leaving the country on the twenty-first for six weeks and Dr. Mbeki has agreed her abatacept can be given early. Her dose depends on her weight band, pharmacy says the vials on the shelf are a mix of good, short-dated, and one that was pulled after a temperature issue, and Meridian has quoted two delivery dates. I need to know whether we can dose her before she travels, on what day, and at what cost, and whether the short-dated stock could be used instead. Rebook her appointment accordingly and draft the note for the rheumatology nurse.",
